# db2_ecm_health_check.sh — Design Context

## What This Document Is

A complete record of the architecture knowledge, design decisions, expert reasoning,
and engineering constraints that shaped `db2_ecm_health_check.sh`. Intended as the
reference document for anyone maintaining or extending the script.

---

## The Stack Being Monitored

**IBM Content Manager 8.7.4** running on **Db2 LUW 11.5 / RHEL 8.x**

### Nine-Database Architecture

```
CNAVDB  ──────────────────────────────────────  IBM Content Navigator (UI)
                                                 Single instance, no HADR
                                                 Session data only — not content

ICMNLSDB  ────────────────────────────────────  ICM Primary Metadata DB
                                                 HADR: primary + standby (NEARSYNC)
                                                 ACR enabled, no Read on Standby
                                                 SINGLE POINT OF FAILURE for entire stack

RMDBAL ◄──── replicates ────► RMDBOM  ────────  Local Disk Resource Manager pair
                                                 Application-level replication (ICM RM layer)
                                                 Not Db2 HADR — row counts must match within ~2%
                                                 Each has its own Db2 HADR pair
        │
        └──────── both migrate ────────────────► RMDBS3  ─  Hitachi S3 deep storage RM
                                                             Migration target — size must grow
                                                             Has own HADR pair

RMDB  ────────────────────────────────────────  Legacy RM (migrating to RMDBS3)
                                                 Size must shrink over time
                                                 No HADR — transitional only
                                                 No SA MP cluster — not HA protected

SIBDB  ───────────────────────────────────────  SA MP quorum DB for RMDBAL+RMDBOM cluster
SIBDBS3  ─────────────────────────────────────  SA MP quorum DB for RMDBS3 cluster
                                                 Near-zero activity (<20 tables, <10k rows each)
                                                 Silent failure = next outage requires manual failover
```

### Dependency Chain (top-down)

ICMNLSDB is the root dependency. Everything flows from it. ICN failure = UI outage only,
no content integrity impact. SIBDB failure is silent — the RM cluster keeps running but
loses automated failover.

