## Critical Architecture Facts

### RMDB_ALPHA / RMDB_OMEGA Replication

- Replication is **ICM application-layer**, not Db2 HADR
- ICM Storage Manager writes to both databases simultaneously
- Db2 layer just stores what RM tells it
- Row count divergence between RMDBAL and RMDBOM is an ICM problem detectable from Db2
- `SYSCAT.TABLES.CARD` total comparison across both databases = replication health signal
- >2% divergence = investigate. >5% = replication likely broken.
- Both databases receive identical write load → similar LOGFILSIZ requirements

### Migration Pipeline

```
RMDB_LEGACY → RMDB_S3  (should show: LEGACY shrinking, S3 growing)
RMDBAL + RMDBOM → RMDB_S3  (local disk migrating to deep storage)
```

If RMDBAL/RMDBOM are growing AND RMDB_S3 is not growing = migration stalled.

### SA MP Clusters

Two independent clusters — two independent scopes of automated failover:

| Cluster | Quorum DB | Governs |
|---------|-----------|---------|
| Cluster 1 | SIBDB | RMDBAL + RMDBOM HADR |
| Cluster 2 | SIBDBS3 | RMDBS3 HADR |

`lssam` output should show two resource groups. One resource group = one cluster
is not configured or has failed silently.

RMDB has no SIBDB — it is a migration source, not HA-protected.

### HADR Configuration

| Database | HADR | Sync Mode | Notes |
|----------|------|-----------|-------|
| ICMNLSDB | Yes | NEARSYNC | ACR enabled, no Read on Standby |
| RMDBAL | Yes | NEARSYNC expected | Each has own pair |
| RMDBOM | Yes | NEARSYNC expected | Each has own pair |
| RMDBS3 | Yes | NEARSYNC expected | Own pair |
| SIBDB | Yes | SYNC acceptable | Near-zero activity |
| SIBDBS3 | Yes | SYNC acceptable | Near-zero activity |
| CNAVDB | No | — | Single instance |
| RMDB | No | — | Legacy/transitional |

### Backup Coordination (15-minute rule)

Backup skew between coordinated pairs creates a window of unresolvable references
on restore. Pairs must be within 15 minutes of each other:

| Pair | Reason |
|------|--------|
| ICMNLSDB ↔ RMDBAL | Metadata + active RM |
| ICMNLSDB ↔ RMDBOM | Metadata + active RM |
| ICMNLSDB ↔ RMDBS3 | Migrated content references |
| RMDBAL ↔ RMDBOM | Replication pair — same point-in-time |
| ICMNLSDB ↔ RMDB | During active migration window |
| ICN | Independent — session data, no content integrity link |
| SIBDB / SIBDBS3 | Independent — cluster state, not content |

### Log Sizing Guidance (LOGFILSIZ in 4KB pages)

| Database | Recommended LOGFILSIZ | Rationale |
|----------|-----------------------|-----------|
| ICMNLSDB | 81920–524288 pages (320MB–2GB per file) | Heavy metadata write load |
| RMDBAL/RMDBOM | 32768–131072 pages (128MB–512MB) | Active RM writes |
| RMDBS3 | 32768–131072 pages (128MB–512MB) | Migration target writes |
| RMDB | 16384 pages (~64MB) | Legacy, minimal writes |
| CNAVDB | 8192 pages (~32MB) | ICN session writes only |
| SIBDB/SIBDBS3 | 4096 pages (~16MB) | SA MP daemon writes only |

